{"url":"/distro/notes-init","slug":"notes-init","collection":"distro","group":"Engineering notes","title":"palm-init notes","description":"palm-init and palmframe-base: what the other pieces need to know.","toc":[{"id":"what-exists","title":"What exists","depth":2},{"id":"for-the-image-builder--recipes","title":"For the image builder / recipes","depth":2},{"id":"services-shipped-in-base","title":"Services shipped in base","depth":2},{"id":"for-palm-login-distrologin","title":"For palm-login (distro/login)","depth":2},{"id":"behaviour-worth-knowing","title":"Behaviour worth knowing","depth":2},{"id":"changed-by-the-installer-integration-2026-10-13","title":"Changed by the installer integration (2026-10-13)","depth":2}],"source":{"path":"distro/notes/init.md","edit":"https://github.com/alexisbcz/palmy/edit/main/distro/notes/init.md","view":"https://github.com/alexisbcz/palmy/blob/main/distro/notes/init.md","generated":[]},"updated":"2026-10-13","hast":["#root",0,["p",0,"Owner of ",["code",0,"distro/init/"],", ",["code",0,"distro/base/"]," and this file."],"\n",["h2",{"id":"what-exists"},"What exists"],"\n",["ul",0,"\n",["li",0,["code",0,"distro/init/"]," — palm-init, PID 1, in Odin. ",["code",0,"distro/init/build.sh"]," builds\n",["code",0,"distro/out/bin/palm-init"],", ",["strong",0,"statically linked"]," (static glibc,\n",["code",0,"-extra-linker-flags:-static"],"). It does not need the dynamic loader or\n",["code",0,"/usr/lib/libc.so.6"]," to start. ",["code",0,"build.sh --test"]," also runs the selftest."],"\n",["li",0,["code",0,"distro/init/test-boot.sh"]," — boots it in QEMU (headless) and drives the\nserial console. Scenarios: ",["code",0,"login"],", ",["code",0,"single"],", ",["code",0,"disk"],", ",["code",0,"all"],"."],"\n",["li",0,["code",0,"distro/base/root/"]," — the files of the ",["code",0,"palmframe-base"]," package."],"\n",["li",0,["code",0,"distro/base/layout"]," — what a plain file tree in git cannot hold: the\nmerged-/usr symlinks, directory modes, non-root owners, ",["code",0,"etc/shadow"]," 0600."],"\n",["li",0,["code",0,"distro/base/apply-layout.sh <rootdir>"]," — copies ",["code",0,"root/"]," and applies\n",["code",0,"layout"],". Run it under fakeroot in the same session as whatever archives\nthe result."],"\n"],"\n",["h2",{"id":"for-the-image-builder--recipes"},"For the image builder / recipes"],"\n",["p",0,"Install palm-init as ",["code",0,"/usr/bin/palm-init"]," and make ",["code",0,"/usr/bin/init"]," a symlink\nto it (",["code",0,"/sbin"]," → ",["code",0,"usr/bin"],", so the kernel finds ",["code",0,"/sbin/init"],"). The kernel\ncommand line needs nothing special: ",["code",0,"root=... ro"]," is fine, palm-init remounts\n",["code",0,"/"]," read-write itself (tested on an ext4 root on virtio-blk mounted ",["code",0,"ro"],")."],"\n",["p",0,"Merged /usr symlinks (also in ",["code",0,"distro/base/layout"],"):"],"\n",["pre",{"class":["shiki","shiki-themes","github-light","github-dark","sk-25qmca"],"tabindex":"0","data-lang":"text"},["code",0,["span",{"class":"line"},["span",{"class":"sk-wvjl67"},"bin       -> usr/bin"]],"\n",["span",{"class":"line"},["span",{"class":"sk-wvjl67"},"sbin      -> usr/bin"]],"\n",["span",{"class":"line"},["span",{"class":"sk-wvjl67"},"lib       -> usr/lib"]],"\n",["span",{"class":"line"},["span",{"class":"sk-wvjl67"},"lib64     -> usr/lib"]],"\n",["span",{"class":"line"},["span",{"class":"sk-wvjl67"},"usr/sbin  -> bin"]],"\n",["span",{"class":"line"},["span",{"class":"sk-wvjl67"},"usr/lib64 -> lib"]],"\n",["span",{"class":"line"},["span",{"class":"sk-wvjl67"},"var/run   -> ../run"]],"\n",["span",{"class":"line"},["span",{"class":"sk-wvjl67"},"var/lock  -> ../run/lock"]],"\n",["span",{"class":"line"},["span",{"class":"sk-wvjl67"},"etc/mtab  -> ../proc/self/mounts"]]]],"\n",["p",0,"Owners that are not root: ",["code",0,"home/palm"]," 1000:1000 (0700), ",["code",0,"home/palm/.profile"],"\n1000:1000, ",["code",0,"var/lib/greeter"]," 900:900 (0750). ",["code",0,"etc/shadow"]," is 0600. ",["code",0,"tmp"]," and\n",["code",0,"var/tmp"]," are 1777."],"\n",["p",0,"busybox applets: one symlink per ",["code",0,"busybox --list"]," name in ",["code",0,"/usr/bin"],". The\nservices use ",["code",0,"/sbin/getty"],", ",["code",0,"/sbin/syslogd"],", and palm-init looks up ",["code",0,"udhcpc"],"\nin ",["code",0,"PATH"]," (",["code",0,"/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin"],"). udhcpc's script is\n",["code",0,"/usr/share/udhcpc/default.script"]," (in base; busybox is configured with that\npath) — it sets the address, default route and ",["code",0,"/etc/resolv.conf"],"."],"\n",["p",0,"A ",["code",0,"palmframe-base"]," PALMBUILD should ship ",["code",0,"distro/base/root/"]," plus ",["code",0,"layout"],"'s\nsymlinks/dirs; whether palm records symlinks and per-file owners is the\nrecipes' and palm's call — ",["code",0,"layout"]," is the list to honour."],"\n",["p",0,["code",0,"/etc/palm/repositories"]," currently says ",["code",0,"/var/lib/palm/repo/x86_64"],". That is a\nguess; the image builder should overwrite it with wherever it puts the\non-disk repository (or an http:// URL)."],"\n",["h2",{"id":"services-shipped-in-base"},"Services shipped in base"],"\n",["table",0,"\n",["thead",0,"\n",["tr",0,"\n",["th",0,"file"],"\n",["th",0,"what"],"\n"],"\n"],"\n",["tbody",0,"\n",["tr",0,"\n",["td",0,["code",0,"getty-ttyS0"]],"\n",["td",0,["code",0,"/sbin/getty -L 115200 ttyS0 vt100"],", ",["code",0,"tty = /dev/ttyS0"]],"\n"],"\n",["tr",0,"\n",["td",0,["code",0,"palm-login"]],"\n",["td",0,["code",0,"/usr/bin/palm-login"],", user root, restart always"],"\n"],"\n",["tr",0,"\n",["td",0,["code",0,"syslog"]],"\n",["td",0,["code",0,"/sbin/syslogd -n -O /var/log/messages"]],"\n"],"\n",["tr",0,"\n",["td",0,"(built-in) ",["code",0,"network"]],"\n",["td",0,["code",0,"udhcpc -i eth0 -b -t 5 -T 2"],", one-shot, only if eth0 and udhcpc exist"],"\n"],"\n"],"\n"],"\n",["p",0,"No getty on tty1: the window manager owns the display; a text getty on the\nsame VT would fight it. ",["code",0,"after = network"]," on a service means \"after udhcpc's\nforeground run\" (lease obtained, or backgrounded after 5 tries)."],"\n",["h2",{"id":"for-palm-login-distrologin"},"For palm-login (distro/login)"],"\n",["ul",0,"\n",["li",0,"palm-init exports ",["code",0,"PALM_AUTOLOGIN=<user>"]," to every service when the kernel\ncommand line has ",["code",0,"palm.autologin=<user>"]," (verified in QEMU). palm-login may\nalso read ",["code",0,"/proc/cmdline"]," itself; both agree."],"\n",["li",0,"palm-login runs as root with ",["code",0,"HOME=/root USER=root PATH=... TERM=linux"],"; its\nstdout/stderr go to ",["code",0,"/var/log/palm-login.log"],", stdin is ",["code",0,"/dev/null"],". It is\na session leader (palm-init calls ",["code",0,"setsid()"]," for every service) but has no\ncontrolling tty. If it needs a VT for the wm, it opens one itself."],"\n",["li",0,"On shutdown palm-init sends SIGTERM to the service's process group (so to\nthe wm and greeter too if they stayed in it), waits 3 s, then SIGKILLs\neverything."],"\n",["li",0,["code",0,"/dev/dri/*"]," is root:video 0660, ",["code",0,"/dev/input/event*"]," root:input 0660 — at\nboot and on hotplug (verified with a QMP-hot-plugged USB keyboard)."],"\n",["li",0,["code",0,"/run"]," is a fresh tmpfs (0755) each boot; ",["code",0,"/run/user/<uid>"]," is palm-login's\nto create."],"\n"],"\n",["h2",{"id":"behaviour-worth-knowing"},"Behaviour worth knowing"],"\n",["ul",0,"\n",["li",0,["code",0,"kill -HUP 1"]," re-reads ",["code",0,"/etc/palm/services"]," and starts services that are\nnew. It does not stop removed ones or restart changed ones."],"\n",["li",0,"A service whose binary is missing or whose user is unknown goes through the\nsame restart backoff (1 s doubling to 30 s) instead of being dropped, so\ninstalling the package later makes it start."],"\n",["li",0,"An unknown key in a service file is an error: the service is not started\nand the console says which line."],"\n",["li",0,["code",0,"palm.single"]," gives a root shell on the console's real tty (from\n",["code",0,"/sys/class/tty/console/active"],", so job control works) and starts nothing\nelse."],"\n",["li",0,"busybox ",["code",0,"poweroff"]," / ",["code",0,"reboot"]," / ",["code",0,"halt"]," work (SIGUSR2 / SIGTERM / SIGUSR1).\nctrl-alt-del is SIGINT → reboot."],"\n"],"\n",["h2",{"id":"changed-by-the-installer-integration-2026-10-13"},"Changed by the installer integration (2026-10-13)"],"\n",["ul",0,"\n",["li",0,["strong",0,"Masks"]," (",["code",0,"service.odin"],"): a service is not started while\n",["code",0,"/etc/palm/services.off/<name>"]," exists (also for the built-in ",["code",0,"network"],").\npalmframe-live ships ",["code",0,"services.off/palm-login"]," and ",["code",0,"services.off/getty-ttyS0"],"\ninstead of the live build deleting palmframe-base's service files, so\n",["code",0,"palm verify"]," on the live system no longer reports them missing. Logged as\n",["code",0,"service X is masked by ..."],". Selftest: 3 mask checks."],"\n"]]}